    "summary": "Box-shaped dish carved of alder, with rectangular outline, curved raised ends, dipping sides, broad rim facing into the dish; the sides and ends are curved in vertical profile. The ends are carved with low relief formline faces - eyes, ears and mouth/beak, with a beaver-like tail in cross hatching between the eyes. The rim at the sides is marked with a single incised line, and the sides with nine knife lines parallel to the corners. The broad rim is inlaid with opercula, missing in five places. The whole still exudes grease, with mould and other detritus on the inside, including some copper salts?",
